.         * OUTCOME VARIABLE
.         * To measure gender equality in household labor for each household an
> d year, we construct an index based on the difference in work hours between p
> artners. The measure ranges from 0 (complete inequality) to 1 (perfect equali
> ty).
.         gen equity = 1 - abs(hours_household - partner_hours_household) / (ho
> urs_household + partner_hours_household)
(13,659 missing values generated)

.         
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3
.         * Our model is a fixed effects panel regression estimating how having
>  a daughter relates to gender equity in household labor within households ove
> r time.
.         * Standard errors are clustered at the household level.
.         * Dependent variable: equity - continuous index measuring equality in
>  household labor between partners (see above)
.         * Key predictor: has_daughter - whether the household has at least on
> e daughter in a given year
.         * Controls: whether the household has any children (has_child), age (
> age), age squared (age2), and number of sons and daughters (numbersons, numbe
> rdaughters).
.         xtreg equity has_daughter has_child age age2 numbersons numberdaughte
> rs, fe cluster(cid)

